<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<diagram program="umlet" version="15.1">
  <zoom_level>10</zoom_level>
  <element>
    <id>Text</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>20</x>
      <y>10</y>
      <w>2000</w>
      <h>40</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>fontsize=20
*Gallean world AI – what happens in one AI turn*</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>Text</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>20</x>
      <y>45</y>
      <w>2000</w>
      <h>30</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>fontsize=12
src/Gallean.Engine/World/Ai · one action per call, repeated until the AI ends its turn</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLClass</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>20</x>
      <y>100</y>
      <w>380</w>
      <h>97</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>*Start of the AI's turn*
--
the game calls WorldAiController.DecideAction
once per action; the AI's memory carries
orders and per-turn counters between calls
halign=left
bg=#cfe8cf
fontsize=12</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLClass</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>20</x>
      <y>250</y>
      <w>380</w>
      <h>97</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>*Step 1  Set orders*
(WorldAiOrderPlanner)
--
every own army gets an order for this action:
what it is trying to do right now
halign=left
bg=#cfe8cf
fontsize=12</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLClass</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>20</x>
      <y>400</y>
      <w>380</w>
      <h>142</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>*Step 2  Spend*
(playable races only)
--
score every economy action, take the best;
if it can be done → do it, back to Step 1
if the best one CAN'T be done → nothing is
bought this step (no fallback to the 2nd best)
= how the AI saves up
halign=left
bg=#cfe8cf
fontsize=12</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLClass</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>20</x>
      <y>625</y>
      <w>380</w>
      <h>127</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>*Step 3  Move armies*
--
for each own army (not in a rioting city,
not marked done this turn):
score every army action under its order,
take the best that can be done → do it
nothing to do → army marked done
halign=left
bg=#cfe8cf
fontsize=12</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLClass</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>20</x>
      <y>850</y>
      <w>380</w>
      <h>67</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>*End turn*
--
all armies done, or 100 actions used
halign=left
bg=#cfe8cf
fontsize=12</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLClass</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>560</x>
      <y>100</y>
      <w>380</w>
      <h>157</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>*Orders the AI gives itself*
(for armies with the Normal order, first match wins)
--
1. Heal: hit points below 80 % (kept until 90 %)
2. Explore: rod planter or thief leader
3. Reinforce: party filled below 80 % of the
    leader's leadership → go to the own city where
    buying units helps, or stay in the city it is in
4. Normal: everything else
halign=left
bg=#dbe7f6
fontsize=12</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLClass</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>560</x>
      <y>380</y>
      <w>380</w>
      <h>97</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>*Orders from the map*
--
Stand · Guard · Defend city/location/army
Move to location · Attack army · Berserk ...
set in the scenario: kept as they are
halign=left
bg=#dbe7f6
fontsize=12</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLClass</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>560</x>
      <y>540</y>
      <w>380</w>
      <h>172</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>*Where an army moves*
(MoveAction, by order)
--
Normal: known enemies, ruins, bags;
    nothing known → explore
Reinforce: only to its target city
    (already there → no move)
Heal: to an own city
Explore: into unexplored land
Map orders: follow their own rule
halign=left
bg=#dbe7f6
fontsize=12</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLClass</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>1100</x>
      <y>100</y>
      <w>380</w>
      <h>217</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>*Economy actions*
(higher priority always wins)
--
P4  Cast spell
P3  Research spell
P2  Hire leader   wants 1 fighter per own
    city + 1 explorer, rod planter, thief;
    short by ≤ 400 gold → 'save up' plan
P1  Construct building   1 per turn
    order: healing, guild, units, spells
P0  Buy unit      1 per turn, into the city
    garrison (AutoFit then moves it into
    the army standing in the city)
halign=left
bg=#fff0a8
fontsize=12</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLClass</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>1100</x>
      <y>400</y>
      <w>380</w>
      <h>97</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>*Unit purchase score*
--
affordable · melee preferred · not the
same unit again · free room in the city
· own army waiting in the city
halign=left
bg=#fff0a8
fontsize=12</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLClass</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>1640</x>
      <y>100</y>
      <w>380</w>
      <h>187</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>*Army actions*
(higher priority always wins)
--
P6  Use item
P5  Resurrect units (in a city)
P4  Heal units (in a city)
P3  AutoFit: garrison units into the party
P2  Attack · Thief · Rod · Enter city ·
    Take bag
P1  Move
P0  Change order
halign=left
bg=#f6dfc4
fontsize=12</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLClass</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>1640</x>
      <y>330</y>
      <w>380</w>
      <h>127</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>*Attack score*
--
only targets it has explored; estimates
the battle first (WorldAiEstimator) and
skips fights its power can't win; weighs
victory, survival, units and XP kept or
lost, distance, target interest/priority
halign=left
bg=#f6dfc4
fontsize=12</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLClass</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>1100</x>
      <y>540</y>
      <w>380</w>
      <h>112</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>*How a plan is scored*
--
WorldAiActionScore = (Priority, Value)
priority compared first; Value 0–1000 is
the product of the action's considerations
(utility curves)
halign=left
bg=#e6e6e6
fontsize=12</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLClass</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>1640</x>
      <y>540</y>
      <w>380</w>
      <h>127</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>*What the AI knows*
--
only explored tiles count as targets (fog)
map goals ('objectives') come only from
scenario events that win the game, and only
from turn 60/50/40/30 (easy → very hard)
custom maps have no events → no goals
halign=left
bg=#e6e6e6
fontsize=12</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>1640</x>
      <y>800</y>
      <w>380</w>
      <h>110</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Legend
green = turn loop
blue = orders and movement
yellow = spending
orange = army actions
grey = scoring and knowledge
fontsize=12</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
